.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
tr
- transliterate, delete or squeeze characters
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
tr [ -cds ] [ string1 [ string2 ] ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Tr copies standard input to standard output, replacing or deleting
selected characters.  Each character of string1 is replaced by the
character in the same position of string2; a character of string1
with no counterpart is deleted.  Ranges (a-z) and the octal escapes
\\nnn are understood in both strings.
.sp
.bd
-c
.sp
Complement the set of characters in string1.
.sp
.bd
-d
.sp
Delete the characters of string1.
.sp
.bd
-s
.sp
Squeeze repeated characters named in string2 to a single one.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
ed (1), m4 (1)
